<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Volume [3D] Sampling (Mesh)</span></h1>
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>This command is accessible from <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Mesh &gt; Volume Sampling [ 3D ]</b></span>.</p>
<p class="description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Volume Sampling</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command fits a cubic grid to the visible selected mesh extents. It modifies the selection by re-sampling at the specified interval in U, V, and W directions of this grid. In each cube of the grid one point is kept. If there are several points near the sample position, the nearest one is used. The resulting entity is point cloud.</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><img src="../mesh/commands_files/volume_sampling.gif" width="257px" height="165px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Distance</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Re-sampling interval in</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>U</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">,</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>V</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">,</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>W</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">. Default value is 0.1mm</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Keep original mesh data</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">If checked, a new point cloud entity is created from the selection and the original data are kept. Otherwise the resulting point cloud replaces the original data. Default value is point cloud replaces the selection.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command works on partial selection as well as on wholly selected entity. If Create as new entity is unchecked, the whole entity will be destroyed, no matter if is selected partially or wholly. If</span> <span class="Command">Volume sampling</span> <span lang="EN-GB">is applied to several entities, it generates single point cloud from their selections. In case selections extents do not overlap, function works only on the selected data with highest volume based on extents.</span></p>
